---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, RESUME_MAILTO } from '../site';
---
<Base title="About" description="About Leon Wu: data scientist for product, growth and revenue, who builds AI tools for data.">
  <div class="about">
    <img src="/leon.jpg" alt="Portrait of Leon Wu" width="667" height="1000" class="photo" />
    <div>
      <h1>About</h1>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          I grew up in New Jersey, went west to UC San Diego, and came back to New York. I started out in
          finance and business, found programming, and ended up with a degree in probability and statistics.
          That combination still shapes how I work: I start from the question, not the model.
        </p>
        <p>
          My day job is the questions companies make money on: what users actually do, who should pay, at what price,
          and whether the revenue number is right. I did that for agency clients at Rauxa, for finance at Indeed (revenue
          forecasts and customer lifetime value), and now for product, growth and monetization at Replit, where I was one
          of the first two people on the data team.
        </p>
        <p>
          The other half of my work is making that kind of answer self-serve. At Indeed I prototyped a Text-to-SQL
          assistant in January 2023, and it grew into a 10-person team. At Replit I led Oracle, our internal analytics agent.
          It sits on a semantic layer the whole company agrees on, and it replaced Hex and Amplitude, saving seven figures a year.
        </p>
        <p>
          The work I'm proudest of rarely looks like a model. It's usually one well-framed question, a careful
          look at what users actually do, and a tool that means nobody has to ask me again.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section aria-labelledby="off">
    <h2 class="kicker" id="off">Off the clock</h2>
    <p>
      Chess, guitar, and too many hours of League of Legends and Riftbound. I'm a Lakers, Man City and Broncos fan, which
      is a lot of emotional variance to carry.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="contact">
    <h2 class="kicker" id="contact">Contact</h2>
    <p>
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>{' · '}<a href={SITE.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a>{' · '}<a href={SITE.github}>GitHub</a>{' · '}<a href={RESUME_MAILTO}>Request my resume</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .about + section { margin-top: 4.5rem; }
  .about { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 9rem 1fr; gap: 2rem; align-items: start; }
  .photo { width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 6px; filter: grayscale(0.15); }
  .about h1 { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .about .prose { font-size: 1.15rem; }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .about { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .photo { width: 7rem; }
  }
</style>
